WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.969
Rhiannon: How can we tell
if someone is being bullied?

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.560
Leah: If a child’s belongings are
forever getting 'lost' or damaged

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.349
or they never seem to have any
money, this may indicate bullying.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.910
If they are suffering from physical
injuries or unexplained bruises, maybe

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.049
they don’t want to go to school or feign
illness, or they are not doing well in

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.390
class, this may also be an indication.

00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:24.210
If they generally become nervous, lose
confidence and become withdrawn, or have

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.789
problems with eating and sleeping this
can be an indication that the child or

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.560
young person could be being bullied.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.020
Rhiannon: Any child can
be bullied for any reason.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.439
If a child is seen as different in
some way or seen as an easy target,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.040
they can be even more at risk.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.430
This might be because of their
race or ethnic background, gender,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.589
sexual orientation or could be just
because they have low self-esteem,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.740
seem shy or introverted or appear
anxious and lack assertiveness.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.970
Leah: They may be bullied for the way they
look, the colour of their hair, if they

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.920
wear glasses or if they have a disability.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.580
Rhiannon: Some may be a target because of
their interests or hobbies, they are new

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.050
to an area, they have changed schools,
or due to their family circumstances.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.950
Leah: Sometimes people can even be bullied
for things we wouldn’t associate with

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.540
bullying, such as being good looking,
popular, clever or having nice things.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.070
Rhiannon: Bullying is all about
causing hurt to others repeatedly,

00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:25.789
with ongoing damaging effects and the
bully gains satisfaction and a sense

00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:27.680
of power, from treating others badly.

00:01:28.639 --> 00:01:32.500
Leah: A young person who becomes visibly
upset at name-calling may increasingly

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.550
become the focus of attention and may
be seen as a soft target, someone who is

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.750
"easy to wind up” but not every at-risk
person will be subject to bullying.

00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:45.890
Rhiannon: Maybe there isn’t a bully
around or maybe the person is more

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.680
self-assured and self-confident and not
as susceptible to bullying in general.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.120
In these cases bullying may not be
the course and we need to look to

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.339
other factors, but it is always worth
being mindful of the possibilities.

